    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "Solve the following. $3x^2+2x-8=0$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-2,\\dfrac43$.\n\nFactorise as $(3x-4)(x+2)=0$ and use the null factor law.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2+2x-8&=3x^2+6x-4x-8\\\\3x^2+2x-8&=3x(x+2)-4(x+2)\\\\3x^2+2x-8&=(3x-4)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(3x-4)(x+2)=0$. By the null factor law, $3x-4=0$ or $x+2=0$.\n$$x=\\frac43\\text{ or }x=-2.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
